 {
  "coord": "1:34",
  "verdict": "FAIL",
  "category": "length",
  "note": "The 53-word \"And as a heavy thing\" sentence can be split easily.",
  "replacement": "MORTON. I am sorry to force you to believe what I wish to God I had not seen. But with these eyes I saw him, bloody, weary and out of breath, returning feeble blows to Harry Monmouth. Monmouth's swift fury beat the never-daunted Percy down to the ground, and he never rose from there alive. In short, his death, whose spirit lent fire even to the dullest peasant in his camp, took fire and heat away from the best-tempered courage in his troops as soon as it was spread about. His side had been steeled by his metal, and once that failed in him, all the rest turned on themselves, like dull, heavy lead. And as a heavy thing, when it is forced, flies with the greatest speed, so our men, weighed down by the loss of Hotspur, lent this weight such lightness with their fear. Arrows did not fly faster toward their target than our soldiers, aiming at their own safety, fled from the field. Then the noble Worcester was taken prisoner, too soon. And that furious Scot, the bloody Douglas, whose hard-working sword had three times killed someone who looked like the King, began to lower his pride. He gave cover to the shame of those who turned their backs, and in his flight, stumbling in fear, he was caught. The sum of it all is that the King has won, and has sent out a swift force to meet you, my lord, under the command of young Lancaster and Westmoreland. That is the news in full."
 },
