 {
  "coord": "2:60",
  "verdict": "FAIL",
  "category": "reversal",
  "note": "\"have at him\" means Falstaff attacks the challenger; \"let him at me\" reverses the attacker.",
  "replacement": "FALSTAFF. My lord, I was born around three o'clock in the afternoon, with a white head and a somewhat round belly. As for my voice, I lost it hollering and singing hymns. I won't offer any more proof of my youth. The truth is, I'm only old in judgment and understanding. And any man who wants to caper with me for a thousand marks, let him lend me the money, and I'll go at him! As for the box on the ear the Prince gave you, he gave it like a rough prince, and you took it like a sensible lord. I've scolded him for it, and the young lion is sorry. Indeed, not in ashes and sackcloth, but in new silk and old sack."
 },
